# Python's own leavings, and the artefacts a local run drops in the tree. The
# databases and the parquet belong in /data inside the container; they land here
# only when something is run against the working tree by hand.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.parquet

# Fitted models. Same story: they live in /data, but a local
# `python -m occupancy_forecast.train` run will drop them here.
*.pkl
models/

# The panel's toolchain. node_modules/ is 69 MB of it and has no business here.
#
# `*/panel/dist/` used to sit on the line below and does not any more: the built
# bundle IS committed, deliberately. DEVELOPMENT.md ("The panel") says why, and
# it is the only copy of that argument.
node_modules/

# Agent instructions specific to the maintainer's machine and authority. The
# shared contract is DEVELOPMENT.md, which IS tracked. Case matters on Linux, so
# this has to be the real spelling -- `claude.md` matches nothing.
CLAUDE.md

# The local demo instance (compose.yaml). `.env` holds one machine's paths and
# LAN address, which is why `.env.example` is the tracked half. The two
# directories are the fictional household's /data and its screenshots -- 25-odd
# MB of archive, parquet and pickles, all of it regenerable by
# `docker compose run --rm instance build|fit|forecasts`.
.env
demo-data/
demo-shots/

# NOT ignored, and deliberately: the STABLE add-on (occupancy-forecast/) is
# generated from occupancy-forecast-edge/ by scripts/promote.sh, but it is
# tracked in full, because it is what the HA box builds and git has to be able
# to say what stable is running. Its config.yaml, DOCS.md and CHANGELOG.md are
# hand-written and the rest is a copy of ../occupancy-forecast-edge. Edit the
# originals there, never the copies here.
